  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.04 Archaeological site",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.04 “Archaeological site” means any location, terrestrial or underwater, where materials made or modified by humans are found such as, but not limited to, aboriginal mounds, forts, earthwork, cellar holes, cemeteries, dams, foundations, villages, camps, quarries, workshops, shipwrecks, mills, factories, and other buildings.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h100.html"
